# ADSP images bundled into the initramfs, globs relative to /usr/lib/firmware.
# USB-C boot needs the ADSP up before the rootfs is mounted (see
# 91armada-adsp): without VBUS sourcing no stick and no keyboard is visible to
# the kernel, and dracut hangs in initqueue.
#
# Which image actually loads is decided per board by the kernel itself: every
# board DT carries its own firmware-name and request_firmware() resolves it.
# The globs below just say "bundle every board's ADSP image", so one generic
# image boots any board whose firmware the repo vendors.
#
# An ADSP image is ~28 MB raw but the initramfs is compressed, so the whole
# set costs far less in the image. A glob matching nothing fails the build.
#
# Not covered: sm8250 boards (thorlite, retroidpocket-common, mangmi, ayaneo
# pocket micro2) reference qcom/sm8250/adsp.mbn, which the repo does not
# vendor; they cannot USB-boot until it is added.

# sm8550, sm8650, sm8750: single ELF image + board DTB, two levels deep
# (ayn/odin2, retroidpocket/rp6, ayaneo/ps2, konkr/pfe, ...).
qcom/sm8550/*/*/adsp.mbn
qcom/sm8550/*/*/adsp_dtb.mbn
qcom/sm8650/*/*/adsp.mbn
qcom/sm8650/*/*/adsp_dtb.mbn
qcom/sm8750/*/*/adsp.mbn
qcom/sm8750/*/*/adsp_dtb.mbn

# sm8550 Ayaneo Pocket: MDT metadata plus split .bNN segments, each requested
# individually by the loader (one level deep under sm8550).
qcom/sm8550/*/adsp.mdt
qcom/sm8550/*/adsp.b*
qcom/sm8550/*/adsp_dtb.mdt
qcom/sm8550/*/adsp_dtb.b*
